  "note": "Four print columns -- name, role, name, role -- at offsets ~28, ~64, ~99 and ~130; the page is read as two name/role pairs split at offset 95. The encoding is mixed: lines 4-6 print ROLE first and the name second ('Principal   Robert McGrath'), while lines 8 onward print the name first and the role second ('Sarah Sabatini   Dept. Liaison'). Lines 4-6 are the administration block and have no heading above them, so their grade_or_dept is ''. Two entries sit under a heading that does not describe them: 'Nick Scoggins  IT Dept.' on line 21 and 'Joanne Poirier  Greenhouse Asst.' on line 22 are separated by white space on the page but the nearest heading above them in their own column is 'Social Studies' and 'Science' respectively, which is what rule 5 records. Their real assignment is the role_raw, not the heading."
